@*
    The page frame every feature shares: measure, a one-line header, and the body.

    WHY THIS EXISTS. Before it, the five feature pages used four different column
    recipes for the same job — `col-lg-7 col-md-9` (Regeneration, Meme),
    `col-lg-8` (Rap Roast results, which did not even match its own setup column),
    `col-lg-5` + `col-lg-7` (Style Director) and `col-lg-4 col-xl-3` + `col-lg-8 col-xl-9`
    (Bulk Generate). Nothing chose those numbers; they accreted.

    The header is one line on purpose. It used to be a glyph bay, the flap title, a
    sentence of description and — on two pages — a three-step "how it works" strip: about
    150px above the first control, restating what the nav link and the Studio row already
    said. The title and the model that will run are the two facts worth the space.
*@
<div class="feature-shell @(Aside is not null ? null : "feature-shell--focused")">

    <header class="feature-head">
        @* The service name sits in flap cells, so arriving on a feature page reads as the
           board turning over to that destination. *@
        <h1 class="feature-page-title"><FlapText Text="@Title" /></h1>
        @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(ModelBadge))
        {
            <span class="badge feature-head__badge">@ModelBadge</span>
        }
    </header>

    @if (Aside is not null)
    {
        @* Split: a setup rail beside the workspace. The rail is first in the DOM, so it is
           also first in the tab order and first on a narrow screen — which is correct, because
           on both you configure before you look at output. *@
        <div class="feature-shell__split">
            <div class="feature-shell__rail">@Aside</div>
            <div class="feature-shell__work">@ChildContent</div>
        </div>
    }
    else
    {
        @ChildContent
    }
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter] public string Title { get; set; } = "Feature";

    /// <summary>The model that will run, e.g. "Gemini". Optional.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? ModelBadge { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The page body, or the workspace half when <see cref="Aside"/> is supplied.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Setup rail. Supplying it selects the split composition.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? Aside { get; set; }
}
